WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.602
-My next guest is
a Grammy-winning artist.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.370
This is her brand-new
holiday album,

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.005
"A Very Trainor Christmas."

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.074
It is out now. It is fantastic.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:10.543
Here is Meghan Trainor!

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.011
Oh, my gosh!

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.714
Look at you. Look, the bow.

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.516
I mean, stop it.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:18.184
Oh, I'm so happy!

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.485
-I'm so pregnant.

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:20.986
-I am so happy.

00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:22.288
And it's wrapped in a bow.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.189
I'm so -- Congratulations.

00:00:24.189 --> 00:00:26.426
Lookit. Oh! Look at this!

00:00:26.426 --> 00:00:27.694
Yeah!

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.429
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.564
How exciting.
-It's real.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.867
-Congratulations.
I'm so excited for you.

00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.669
How are you feeling?

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.837
How has it been being pregnant

00:00:38.837 --> 00:00:41.474
during quarantine
and everything?

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.676
-It was great,
like, not traveling.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.212
And if I felt sick, I'm like,
"Well, at least I'm home,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.280
you know, and doing interviews
like this."

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.016
I was so lucky for that.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:52.418
And then the only bump
in the road I had was

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:56.122
I got gestational diabetes,
but so many women have it.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.657
And it was just,
like, the unknowing.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.658
Like, I didn't know what it was.
-I don't know what it is.

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:01.994
-And it's like a whole --
It's, like, a genetics thing.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:05.064
So my mom had it and she didn't
even give me a full warning.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.834
But it's basically I just
watch what I eat now,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.237
I write everything down, I check
my blood, and we're good now.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.272
I've been crushing it.
It's like a game for me.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:16.142
And I'm winning.
-[ Laughs ] Exactly.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.411
-So it's nice to know
we're both healthy.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.712
-This is great news.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.114
December is a giant month
for you

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:22.982
because your birthday
is coming up.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.416
-Yes, it is.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:27.786
-Which is also the same day of
your wedding anniversary,

00:01:27.786 --> 00:01:30.155
I believe.
-Yep, I did that.

00:01:30.155 --> 00:01:32.859
-Happy birthday.
Happy anniversary.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.027
-Thank you.
-And then Christmas.

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:36.062
How are you going to celebrate

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.497
all these things
without overdoing it?

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:39.532
You got to, like, pace yourself.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.900
-I know.
Everyone is worried this year.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.002
I just told them,
like, get me baby stuff.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.804
That's all I need, you know?
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.372
-I'm just like starting to nest.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.774
He's coming around
early February.

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:49.843
So it'll be perfect.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:51.711
I'll get all my stuff ready.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.680
-Oh, my gosh. I mean, this is --

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.382
this is just gonna be
the best Christmas ever.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:02:00.720
Let's talk about your new album,
"A Very Trainor Christmas."

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.188
This is your first ever
Christmas album.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.190
And I got to tell you,
I love it.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.126
It's a fantastic record,
top to bottom.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.828
It really is a family affair.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.930
The whole family is involved in
this album.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.732
-Yeah, my older brother actually

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:15.101
took that picture
in my living room.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.435
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:18.638
And they wrote all the songs
with me and my brother.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.606
My little brother
produced all the originals,

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:21.707
most of them, with me.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.075
And my dad's playing piano

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:25.010
on "Have Yourself
a Merry Little Christmas."

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:26.779
I got my two cousins
to come over.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.281
And I told them, "I'm pregnant.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:30.249
Also sing backgrounds
on 'Rudolph.'"

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.451
You know?
It was a big family project.

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:34.053
-How awesome is that?

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:37.323
It is 18 songs.
It is jam-packed.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.992
I mean, you get your money's
worth with this one.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.226
It's classics.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.595
-But there's also
some covers on here of, like,

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:44.530
you know --
I mean, there's brand-new ones.

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.265
But there's also covers.

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:49.401
"It's Beginning to Look
a Lot Like Christmas."

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:50.703
"Winter Wonderland."

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.738
"White Christmas" with
Seth MacFarlane, by the way,

00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:55.441
is the --
right now, it is number one

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.810
on Billboard's
Adult Contemporary chart.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.846
-Whoo! I know!
-Congratulations on that.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.280
-Number one!

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.383
-That guy is unbelievable too.
He's so talented.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:05.051
-He's so good.
-And funny.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:09.155
But my favorite jam --
can you guess or no?

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:13.392
-Ugh. I don't know. Maybe, um...

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.861
Is it a cover or an original?
-It's a cover.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:18.397
-Okay. Is it "Last Christmas"?

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:19.465
-It's "Last Christmas."

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:22.067
-Oh!

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.669
-No one can cover --
-I got it!

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:27.507
-No one can cover that song
and I go like, "Well, nice try."

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:30.509
This is fantastic, and I love
not only your singing on it,

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.878
but the production
and the way it starts

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:35.381
with like
a "whu-whu-whu-whu-whu-whu-whu"

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:38.718
and then grows up and -- I go --
I love it.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:41.887
I go, "Dude, she hit a home run
with this one."

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:44.123
-I didn't realize how much
pressure that would be.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.192
A lot of people were like,
"I really hate when people cover

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.060
this song,
but you did a great job."

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.996
I was like, "Oh, my God."
-It's a tough one to cover.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.664
I think that one's a tou--
-It's tough.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:52.798
-The other tough one is

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:54.500
The Waitresses'
"Christmas Wrapping."

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.868
You can't really do it.
-Yeah.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.603
-Like The Waitresses did.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:04:00.807
But this one was -- it's --
The whole record is great.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.708
But I love the production
on that.

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.877
Your voice is great.
It's just perfect.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.580
The keyboard. The sound is
just great on that one.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.782
I love that.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.685
-The whole -- I just love
Christmas albums too.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.853
-Yeah, I love what you do
with Dolly.

00:04:14.853 --> 00:04:16.723
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my gosh.
-Queen Dolly Parton.

00:04:16.723 --> 00:04:17.756
It's great!

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:18.857
-We'll talk about that
some other time.

00:04:18.857 --> 00:04:20.325
I was sweating bombs.

00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:21.794
I go, "I can't sing this song."

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.363
What's wrong with people?
But it was so much fun.

00:04:24.363 --> 00:04:26.399
It's Dolly. It was the best.
-Yeah.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:27.933
-But then you get -- you go,

00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:30.335
"Great, here's a new song
called 'Holidays,'

00:04:30.335 --> 00:04:32.238
and here's Earth, Wind &amp; Fire."

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.873
And I go --

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.008
It's just brilliant.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:37.810
How'd the collaboration
come about?

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.279
-I heard that -- they've
always been so nice to me,

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:41.914
but I heard they
would be willing to do

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.416
a duet with me on this album.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.317
And I was like,
"It has to be an original.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:49.188
And I have to show my heroes
like, 'You raised me.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:50.423
You taught me what music is.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.824
I'm going to make you proud.'"

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.926
And I got with
my two favorite musicians,

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:55.728
Mike Sabath, Eddie Benjamin.

00:04:55.728 --> 00:04:57.897
They're children.
They're like 20 years old.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:05:01.200
And we all, like,
got together -- tested --

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.169
we're all safe -- got together,

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.570
and we wrote this song
in an evening,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.271
and we're like, "We just want it
to be a party."

00:05:06.271 --> 00:05:08.641
We studied their music.
We played it all day.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.510
-It's very Earth, Wind &amp; Fire
but perfectly you.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.845
Perfectly you too
'cause I was like --

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:15.681
[ Vocalizes ]
Dude, I was --

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.583
I mean, you know.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:20.252
-We were like, "We have to have
a horn section, a breakdown."

00:05:20.252 --> 00:05:22.955
Like, it was math.
-Yeah. But I love the song.

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:24.624
And you're performing it
for us tonight,

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:27.126
which I'm very excited
and thankful for.

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.162
We're very in the theme
this year.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.530
So I'm so thankful for that.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.767
But first, you're always up for
doing something fun on our show,

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.168
which we love about you.

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:37.903
When we come back,
you and I are going to play

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:41.006
a musical game called
"Google Translate Songs."

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:42.808
More with Meghan Trainor
when we come back.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.911
Stick around, everybody!
-Whoo!

